{"title":"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Joyce has two identical jars. The first jar is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> full of water and contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> mL of water. The second jar is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> full of water. How much water, in mL, does the second jar contain?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> of a jar is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> mL, and because the first jar has 3 times as much water as the second jar (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9d84d1f676643369c2236664accbe4b80d8263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{3}{4}}{\\frac{1}{4}}=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"50\" height=\"49\" />), then the second jar has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/5/c05d6d6d1068a5111df5dea3362059ec1ebaba9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{300}{3}=\\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" /> mL of water.\n</p><p>~originally by Baihly2024\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdcb968f4f3d2e0d78a67fedc92a8d31183b2436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/9/b899aba26cc33f0026125daebb44a60349c999b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> mL of water, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0a97c38b875cf580d8fc1f0fd153f834140804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac34\\div3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/aced23c94fd429579ca66f262a31767cca812edd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300\\div3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> mL of water, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cd0f9f9869b39e79527f9010293adf7bfe5210f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> mL of water, so the second jar has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43bc38a3aa247c41492f0162a7f4b8cc4ef1c108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> mL of water.\n</p><p>~Yuhao2012\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018010902\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.016 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 69/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2452/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.924      1 2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    5.924      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35908:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018010902 and revision id 279286. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}